  "id": "Compound::DB00126 - Gene::5352",
  "verbalization": "Vitamin C is implicated in the interaction with Plod2 through a series of molecular pathways that involve the enzyme Plod1 and its related activities. The evidence suggests that Vitamin C binds to Plod1, which then participates in the catalytic activity of prolyl- and peptidyl-lysine 5-dioxygenase, both of which are involved in the modification of collagen. This indicates that Vitamin C may influence the activity of Plod1, potentially affecting the production or modification of collagen-related proteins. Additionally, Vitamin C also binds to Ogfod2, which is involved in the binding of L-ascorbic acid, and this interaction is linked to Plod2. While the direct relationship between Vitamin C and Plod2 is not explicitly stated, the evidence suggests a possible indirect connection through the involvement of Plod1 and Ogfod2 in the regulation of collagen-related processes. The mechanisms highlight a potential role of Vitamin C in modulating the activity of enzymes involved in collagen synthesis, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of this relationship.",
